  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  newTitle: Title - Natural selection
  newAuthor: 
  newDesc: Natural selection is a mechanism of evolution. Organisms that are more
    adapted to their environment are more likely to survive and pass on the genes
    that aided their success. This process causes species to change and diverge over
    time.  Natural selection is one of the ways to account for the millions of species
    that have lived on Earth.
