  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  newTitle: Title- Exoplanets
  newAuthor: 'Author - Google '
  newDesc: "An exoplanet is any planet beyond our solar system. Most orbit other
    stars, but free-floating exoplanets, called rogue planets, orbit the galactic
    center and are untethered to any star.Most of the exoplanets discovered so far
    are in a relatively small region of our galaxy, the Milky Way. We know from NASA\u2019s
    Kepler Space Telescope that there are more planets than stars in the galaxy."
--- !u!64 &1497652827
